[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67496,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mesenchymal cardiac hamartoma is a myocardial collection of mature, irregularly arranged mesenchymal tissues normally found within the heart.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67497,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67498,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F01 Benign neoplasm of intrathoracic organs</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67499,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> cardiac hamartoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67500,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67501,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mesenchymal cardiac hamartomas occur in both the septum and the free walls of the ventricles.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67502,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mesenchymal cardiac hamartomas may be associated with dyspnoea, fatigue, or syncope. Ventricular arrhythmias and sudden death have been reported.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67503,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cases in adult men and women have been reported.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67504,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown. Although few data exist, the lesion is probably congenital in origin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67505,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No genetic or syndromic predispositions have been identified.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67506,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion appears as a soft tissue mass involving the endocardium, myocardium, or epicardium. It may protrude into the cardiac chamber. Grossly, mesenchymal hamartomas are tan or pink in colour and may shell out easily, but the lesion has infiltrative borders that extend irregularly into the adjacent myocardium on microscopy. Neither gross necrosis nor calcifications are typically present {20850353}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67507,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion contains an admixture of mature tissues including irregularly arranged cardiomyocytes, smooth muscle cells, fibroblasts, blood vessels (veins, arteries, arterioles, venules, and capillaries), nerves, fibrous tissue, and adipose tissue. Scattered inflammatory cells, such as lymphocytes and macrophages, may be seen. The low mitotic activity, as well as the lack of necrosis and cytological atypia, is consistent with the benign nature of these lesions. The cardiac myocytes may have nuclear hypertrophy, sarcoplasmic degenerative changes (myocytolysis), and haphazard arrangement. The vessels may have intimal myxoid narrowing and be inflamed.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry shows variable reactivity with desmin and MSA (smooth and cardiac muscle), SMA (smooth muscle), troponin (cardiac muscle), S100 (fat and nerves), CD31 and factor&nbsp;VIII (vascular endothelium), cytokeratin AE1/AE3 (focal endothelial cells), and lymphoid and macrophage markers in areas of inflammation (CD3, CD20, CD68, and others) {29103814}.</p>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes fibroma, rhabdomyoma, hamartoma of mature cardiac myocytes, mature teratoma, lipoma, and vascular hamartoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67508,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not described</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67509,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67510,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Discrete collection of mature mesenchymal tissues in the heart</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Ventricular involvement</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67511,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67512,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 305,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis is not definitively known, owing to the rarity of the lesion and its relatively new description. Mesenchymal cardiac hamartomas may be surgically excised. Although the margins may seem clear grossly, they are seldom clear histologically; however, the implication of this for recurrence is not yet known.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]